+## Design Document
+
+### Overview
+This document analyzes schedule conflict detection mechanisms in the Tonebox music education management system.
+
+### Core Conflict Types
+
+#### 1. Teacher Time Conflict
+- **Detection Point**: [lesson_booking.py:check_time_conflict()](file:///app/lesson_schedule/lesson_booking.py#L45-L70)
+- **Logic**: When scheduling a lesson, the system checks if the teacher has any existing lessons at the same time slot on the same day.
+- **Time Overlap Formula**: `new_start < existing_end AND new_end > existing_start`
+- **Excluded Statuses**: `cancelled`, `no_show`
+
+#### 2. Room Booking Conflict
+- **Detection Point**: [booking_manager.py](file:///app/music_bookings/booking_manager.py)
+- **Logic**: Prevents double-booking of studio rooms for the same time slot.
+
+#### 3. Lesson Capacity Conflict
+- **Detection Point**: [booking_manager.py:check_lesson_capacity()](file:///app/music_bookings/booking_manager.py#L47-L59)
+- **Logic**: Ensures the number of bookings does not exceed `Lesson.max_students`.
+
+### Conflict Resolution Strategy
+1. **Priority-based**: Earlier bookings take precedence
+2. **Graceful rejection**: Returns HTTP 409 Conflict with descriptive error message
+3. **Cross-validation**: Validates instrument availability, teacher availability, and room availability
+
+### Future Enhancements
+- [ ] Implement recurring lesson conflict detection
+- [ ] Add buffer time between lessons
+- [ ] Support for multi-room conflict detection
+- [ ] Real-time availability suggestion API
